course: dictionary
lesson: 6284
title: The word month
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A month is one of the twelve parts of a year, like March or July. A year has 12 months. A month is also a time of about four weeks, as in «in a month».
explain: Use the words around month to find its meaning. «Fixed costs are bills that come every month, like rent, energy and council tax.» The word every tells you these bills come again and again, once in each month. Check it by swapping in a meaning: "every four weeks" still makes sense.
explain: Month often has a small signal word before or after it. «Once a month» means one time in each month. «A month ago» means about four weeks back. Read the words next to month to work out what it means in that sentence.
fact: A year has 12 months.
fact: A month has about 30 days, or about 4 weeks.
fact: Some months have 31 days, and February has 28 or 29.
fact: «Once a month» means one time in each month.
fact: In science, the Moon goes round the Earth in about a month.
exercise: «A year has 12 months.» How many months are in a year? | 30 | 10 | *12 | 4
exercise: «A credit card bill shows what was spent that month.» What does that month mean here? | The month after the bill arrives, always | *The month when the spending was made | A bill of 60 pounds | Any day of the year at all
exercise: «If you save £50 every month, you have saved £100 after two months.» How much has been saved after two months? | £200 | £25 | £50 | *£100
test: «Some months have 31 days, and February has 28 or 29.» Which month has the fewest days? | *February | March | December | July
test: «Once a month» means how often? | Every day | Every hour | *One time in each month | Once a year
exam: Ella reads, «After a few months, he had ringing in his ears that would not go away.» What does after a few months mean? | After exactly one year | After one minute | *After several months have passed | Before he started practising
